{"repositoryId":1166341984,"availability":"available","full":"jagduvi1/Cellarion","name":"Cellarion","description":"A modern wine cellar app for tracking bottles, values, and collections.","category":"Other","language":"JavaScript","stars":25,"forks":10,"created":"2026-02-25T05:51:10Z","updated":"2026-10-15T14:22:59Z","license":"AGPL-3.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://cellarion.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://cellarion.app/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T15:00:59.042Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T15:00:59.042Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T15:00:59.042Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-15T15:00:59.042Z","stars":25,"forks":10}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Cellarion is a hosted wine cellar app — a ready-to-use online service at cellarion.app. Create a free account and start tracking your bottles, organizing them into cellars and racks, searching a shared wine registry, getting sommelier-curated drink-window recommendations, and chatting with an AI sommelier about your collection. No installation, no server, no setup — just sign up and go. Every feature is free, forever.","Just want to use Cellarion? Go to cellarion.app and sign up. You do not need to clone this repository, run Docker, or host anything yourself. There's also a public demo account (Try the demo on the landing page) and an Android app on Google Play.","Cellarion is also open-source (AGPL-3.0), so if you'd prefer to run your own private instance, you can self-host it. The rest of this README covers self-hosting — see Quick Start. Most people should just use the hosted service at cellarion.app."],"features":["Bottle tracking — Log every bottle with vintage, producer, region, price, rating, and tasting notes; add more of a bottle you already own in one click","Cellar & rack management — Multiple cellars with customizable rack grids (up to 20×20) and a 3D cellar room view for physical placement","Offline mode — Keeps a copy of your cellars, racks and bottles on the device, so the app works in the cellar with no signal: browse, find a bottle in its rack, consume/open/pour, place and move bottles, edit notes and…","Reserved bottles — Mark bottles as \"spoken for\" (a birthday, a dinner) so suggestions and consume flows respect them","Drink-window alerts — Sommelier-curated maturity windows per wine and vintage; alerts when bottles approach peak, are in window, or slipping past it"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jagduvi1/Cellarion/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"7c3385e28115875f2c160205ba86a46a566a16b777e60ab17acabca759411e11","extractedAt":"2026-10-15T15:00:59.386Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T15:00:59.386Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Cellarion is a hosted wine cellar app — a ready-to-use online service at cellarion.app. Create a free account and start tracking your bottles, organizing them into cellars and racks, searching a shared wine registry, getting sommelier-curated drink-window recommendations, and chatting with an AI sommelier about your collection. No installation, no server, no setup — just sign up and go. Every feature is free, forever.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jagduvi1/Cellarion/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Create a free account and start tracking your bottles, organizing them into cellars and racks, searching a shared wine registry, getting sommelier-curated drink-window recommendations, and chatting with an AI sommelier about your collection.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jagduvi1/Cellarion/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"hosting","status":"documented","text":"Cellarion is also open-source (AGPL-3.0), so if you'd prefer to run your own private instance, you can self-host it.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jagduvi1/Cellarion/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Create an account and start using the full service today — every feature 